.page logger 1 write a message into the kernel log

# SYNOPSIS
*logger* [*-t* _TAG_] _MESSAGE_...

# DESCRIPTION
`logger` joins its arguments with single spaces and writes them as one line into the kernel log, where `dmesg` shows them and the serial console prints them. The line is tagged with the name of the program unless `-t` gives another tag. Lines longer than about 200 characters are cut.

# OPTIONS
@ *-t* _TAG_
    Use _TAG_ instead of `logger` as the tag of the line.

# EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if there is no message.

# EXAMPLES
    logger backup finished
    logger -t cron nightly job done
    dmesg | tail -2

# SEE ALSO
dmesg(1), gensokyo(7)
